# No commit co-authors

When creating git commits:

- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by:` trailers (including `Cursor` / `cursoragent@cursor.com`).
- Do **not** add `Made-with: Cursor` or similar attribution lines.
- Pass only the intended subject/body via HEREDOC. If a tool or hook appends a co-author, strip it before finishing (amend **only** when the user asked to commit and the amend rules allow it).
- Never force-push to rewrite co-authors unless the user explicitly asks.

This applies to every commit in this repo and should be treated as a hard requirement.
